{"file":"picker-1440-light.png","ok":true,"unit":{"lab":{"found":true,"text":"%","caps":"normal","ls":"-1.0472px","style":"italic","color":"oklch(0.289468 0.00386159 34.63)","px":"23.0384px"},"oklch":{"found":true,"text":"deg","caps":"normal","ls":"-1.0472px","style":"italic","color":"oklch(0.289468 0.00386159 34.63)","px":"23.0384px"}},"consoleHue":["oklch(95.832172477266% 0.272450443952 9.83402284231deg / 82.7%) — Color Picker","@layer fouc-guard {\n                .hidden { display: none; }\n                body {\n                    background-color: var(--saved-bg);\n                    background-image: linear-gradient(\n                        135deg,\n                        var(--saved-bg-0) 0%,\n                        var(--saved-bg-1) 33%,\n                        var(--saved-bg-2) 67%,\n                        var(--saved-bg-3) 100%\n                    );\n                }\n            }","/* Fonts loaded via <link> tags in index.html to avoid render-blocking @import */\n\n/* `.pastel-rainbow-text` EXCISED (S.W5-7 · Q4 RATIFIED EXCISE 2026-07-05;\n * the `--accent-live` ramp alternative NOT taken): the fixed six-hue candy\n * ramp failed contrast at every stop over the light header wash (≈1.1–1.5:1),\n * ignored the per-view accent axis, and was the page's only rainbow moment —\n * decoration, not information. The three consumers (PalettesPane heading,\n * DockViewSelect palettes entry, PaletteDialog header) speak ink. */\n\n/* The ONE loading-ink recipe (S.W5 Lane A / W5-1 — the `ec1b200` register,\n * modernized): every skeleton surface in the app reads this single muted-ink\n * family through glass-ui's `--skeleton-glass-bg` seam — one `color-mix`,\n * both schemes, opaque enough to read as SHADOW against the field, never as\n * content. The `--skeleton-shimmer-tint` line is the letter-L9 producer seam\n * (the sheen joins the same ink family once glass-ui's `::after` reads it).\n * Consumers: ShadowPalette + PaletteCardSkeleton (both `bg-well`),\n * AdminListSkeleton + the admin tag-chip shadows (resting plate).\n *\n * E1-R2 (T.W8 remediation_1): the former `color-mix(muted-foreground 22%,\n * muted)` recipe was NOT certified against its ground — in dark it landed ≈\n * `--well-bg` (probed ΔL 0.007, seg-vs-well 1.02:1), collapsing the ghost to a\n * featureless slab. The ink is now a CERTIFIED tone-step OF the well ground\n * itself: a fixed φ-ish fraction of `--foreground` mixed into `--well-bg`, so\n * the block is guaranteed a bounded ΔL from the well in BOTH schemes by\n * construction (darker than the well in light, lifted above it in dark — the\n * scheme-adaptive direction falls out of the token, no per-scheme fork), and\n * the genesis \"muted blocks\" read as BLOCKS against every neutral skeleton\n * ground (well ≈ resting plate). Low-chroma by construction (both `--well-bg`\n * and `--foreground` are near-neutral), so the muted-family character holds. */\n\n.skeleton-ink-register {\n    --skeleton-ink-pole: var(--foreground);\n    --skeleton-ink: color-mix(in oklab, var(--well-bg), var(--skeleton-ink-pole) 15%);\n    --skeleton-glass-bg: var(--skeleton-ink);\n    --skeleton-shimmer-tint: color-mix(in srgb, var(--muted-foreground) 24%, transparent);\n}\n\n/* X-DS value pass 4 (P4R-04): the one tone step keeps its 15 %, but it RECEDES\n * in both schemes. In dark the foreground is cream, so a step toward it lifted\n * the ghost above the plate (the brightest slab on Extract's empty card, louder\n * than the verb that fills it); dark steps toward the page background instead. */\n\n.dark .skeleton-ink-register {\n    --skeleton-ink-pole: var(--background);\n}\n\n/* The SPECIMEN ink walk (S.W5-1's `specimen` register, FINALLY consumed —\n * T.W3-2 · D9): a low-chroma hue rotation around the live accent (fixed 36°\n * steps, C clamped to 0.12) mixed INTO the ink base so the ghost stays\n * shadow-first, per-segment via `--i`. Lifted here from PaletteCardSkeleton's\n * scoped block the day it gained a second consumer (DESIGN.md's\n * global-utility rule): the ShadowPalette true-empty ghost (STILL) reads it\n * as fill; the developing skeleton's strip seams read it through glass-ui's\n * `--skeleton-glass-bg`. Guarded: engines without relative-color calc() keep\n * the plain ink base (the recipe never falls to transparent). */\n\n.specimen-seg {\n    --specimen-ink: var(--skeleton-ink);\n}\n\n@supports (color: oklch(from red calc(l) c calc(h + 36deg))) {\n    .specimen-seg {\n        --specimen-ink: color-mix(\n            in oklab,\n            var(--skeleton-ink) 78%,\n            oklch(from var(--accent-live) l 0.12 calc(h + var(--i, 0) * 36deg))\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/* Dashed inset well — the recessed container that collects an in-progress set\n * of colors (the current-palette editor; the mix \"Selected\" tray left it for\n * the bare-section grammar at X-DS pass 9, V9C-05). Both sites\n * used `.dashed-well` as a never-defined phantom (inv-N-7); this mints the\n * intended affordance in house tokens: a dashed-bordered, faintly-recessed\n * column that visually groups its swatch row + label, echoing the dashed\n * add-swatch button each well already contains. */\n\n.dashed-well {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    gap: 0.625rem;\n    padding: 0.75rem;\n    /* R.W4 Lane A / A1 — hairline law 4: the well's dashed edge reads the ONE\n     * `--card-edge` mint (in-house, scheme-stable), never a `--border` fork. */\n    border: 1.5px dashed var(--card-edge);\n    border-radius: var(--radius-card);\n    /* T.W3-1 (D1 rung-2 WELL; supersedes the S-20 glass recipe — R8): an\n     * in-plate fixture is an opaque TONE-STEP of its host plate, never a\n     * second pane of glass — the ONE `--well-bg` token, NO backdrop-blur\n     * (blurring the aurora through the host is the mud generator, RC-3).\n     * The dashed edge ALONE carries the in-progress semantics.\n     * X-DS pass 1 (V1-02): the chip cartoon rung is GONE — a fixture seated\n     * inside a plate casts nothing (the plate already casts the pane's ONE\n     * stamp, and glass's stepped rung fell down-LEFT against it). */\n    background: var(--well-bg);\n}\n\n/* X-DS pass 2 (V2C-13) — ONE DASH PER AFFORDANCE. A well that holds the\n * dashed add-slot (Mix's \"Selected\", the current-palette editor) draws a plain\n * hairline: the add-slot's own dashed silhouette is the empty-slot sign, and a\n * dashed well around it made two dashed outlines for one affordance. A well\n * with no add-slot inside (Extract's empty drop zone) keeps the dashed edge,\n * because there the edge IS the affordance. */\n\n.dashed-well:has(.add-slot-ghost) {\n    border: 1px solid var(--card-edge);\n}\n\n/* THE SEATED SEARCH FIELD (T.W3-3 · T-12 — THE REGISTER LAW: fields on paper\n * wear paper; fields on glass stay glass). glass-ui's `.input-bar` recipe is\n * dock furniture — the FLOATING chrome rung (80/88%-α glass + blur(13px) +\n * a 24rem dock cap + a baked mono voice). Seated in a pane BODY it is the one\n * floating-glass element in a cartoon-grammar column (t-search-tabs §1-3):\n * over a flat plate the blur has nothing to blur, the dark roast reads darker\n * than its own plate, and the cap rags the bar 78px short of its siblings at\n * 1440 AND 768 (t-mobile F-7). This opt-in re-seats the bar on the MATERIAL\n * LADDER as the Z2 in-plate fixture it is (DESIGN.md § Surfaces):\n *\n *   fill    — the ONE rung-2 `--well-bg` tone-step, NO backdrop-blur (RC-3);\n *   edge    — the drawn `--card-edge` ink hairline (the dashed-well's solid\n *             sibling — hairline law 4, ONE edge mint);\n *   stamp   — NONE (X-DS pass 1 · V1-02: a seated fixture casts nothing; the\n *             tone step and the hairline are the whole seat);\n *   measure — the dock cap dies: a seated field runs its host column (ASK-C);\n *   voice   — content-class (the `.input-bar-field` rule below).\n *\n * INTERIM DEMO SEAT — a consumer opt-in on the producer recipe (unlayered, so\n * it wins over the `@layer components` recipe by layer order — the exact\n * mechanism the producer's own `bare` rung proved), NEVER a recipe fork.\n * BOOKED SWAP (T.W3 §BOOKS \"W3-3 interim search seat\"): dies onto glass-ui's\n * P3 seated field-chrome rung — GLASSUI-T-ASKS ASK-D (`variant=\"seated\"`),\n * with ASK-B (the font seam) + ASK-C (the cap seam) — at the adopt event. */\n\n.search-seated {\n    background: var(--well-bg);\n    backdrop-filter: none;\n    border: 1.5px solid var(--card-edge);\n    box-shadow: none;\n    max-width: none;\n}\n\n/* The producer's focus ring, restated unlayered (the unlayered `none` above\n * would otherwise silently beat the layered `.input-bar:focus-within` ring). */\n\n.search-seated:focus-within {\n    box-shadow: var(--focus-ring-shadow);\n}\n\n/* Voice = CONTENT-CLASS (T-12): a prose search field speaks its plate's text\n * voice; the producer's baked `--font-mono` (`components.css:235`, ASK-B's\n * seam target) is a statement about CSS-literal readouts, not prose. Mono\n * stays an EXPLICIT per-field opt-in (SearchFilterBar's color input keeps it\n * by class; identifier fields opt back in the same way). */\n\n.search-seated .input-bar-field {\n    font-family: inherit;\n}\n\n/* The gold ADMIN-identity icon ink (S.W7-1 consume / W7-7 dedup home) — the\n * ONE demo-side gold icon recipe, lifted here because its consumers span\n * components (the Dock.vue wax-seal ink + DockViewSelect's trigger/menu\n * icons; scoped copies were byte-identical twins, god-module census §2.1).\n * The fuller \"ONE gold/admin shimmer primitive\" consolidation stays the\n * filed glass-ui letter L15 ask. */\n\n.gold-shimmer-icon {\n    color: var(--color-gold);\n}\n\n/* Swatch-row list idiom (R.W4 Lane B / B1) — shared by the three swatch\n * TransitionGroups (CurrentPaletteEditor, MixSourceSelector,\n * MixResultDisplay): dots pop in/out on the enter/exit family with\n * scale-only geometry and neighbours reflow on the family move class. A\n * shared recipe (3 consumers) per DESIGN.md's global-utility rule.\n *\n * The leaving dot stays IN FLOW and scales out in its own slot (X.W7.f2 ·\n * MSS-16/MR-35). It is never lifted out with `position: absolute`: Vue writes\n * no coordinates to a leaving element, and CSS Flexbox L1 §4.1 places an\n * abspos child with auto insets as if it were the SOLE flex item — the row's\n * main-start edge, not its former slot — so the lifted dot teleported to the\n * leading edge before it shrank. Fixed here once, never per consumer. */\n\n.swatch-row {\n    --vj-enter-y: 0px;\n    --vj-enter-scale: 0;\n}\n\n/* The plate ink (X.W7.z2 · R-15 ≡ C-11) — the ONE recipe for the plate\n * captions (ImageDropZone, ExtractWorkbench, ExtractControls, EmptyState, and\n * through EmptyState the ErrorBoundary and PaneErrorPlate plates): the\n * certified de-emphasis rung `--ink-muted` (declared at `:root` in\n * foundation.css, boot-stamped live), never the STATIC `text-muted-foreground`\n * that failed the text floor over the live-ambient plate. A shared recipe\n * (4 consumers) per DESIGN.md's global-utility rule; the bare read, no\n * masking fallback. */\n\n.plate-ink {\n    color: var(--ink-muted);\n}\n\n/* THE WELL INK (X-DS pass 1 · V1C-01). V1-03 made `--well-bg` a wash over\n * the live host plate, so the static `--muted-foreground` (tuned for the old\n * opaque cream well) fell to 1.6-2.1:1 inside every well. The token, not the\n * instances, follows the tone: inside a well root the secondary ink is the\n * certified over-plate rung `--ink-muted`, taken one golden step (0.382)\n * further toward `--foreground` — the well's own 8% `--foreground` wash moves\n * the ground toward the ink, so the ink moves away by more (bare `--ink-muted`\n * measured 3.7-3.9:1 on the dark well). Every `text-muted-foreground`,\n * placeholder and icon seated in a well reads it. (V1-17 did the bare rung\n * per-site for the gradient.) */\n\n.dashed-well,\n.console-well,\n.search-seated,\n[data-generate-plate] {\n    --muted-foreground: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ink-muted), var(--foreground) 38.2%);\n}\n\n/* THE SCALAR RANGE INK (X-DS pass 2 · V2C-06 / V2C-09; re-derived at pass 3 ·\n * V3C-04). The app's scalar sliders (glass's default scrubber variant: the\n * config consoles of Atmosphere and Blob, Gradient's Direction, Extract's K and\n * kC before a run develops) fill their range with ONE ink, set once on the\n * token glass's slider reads (`--slider-range-bg`), never per pane. The\n * spectrum sliders (picker channels, the developed K rail, Generate) paint\n * their own track and leave the range transparent by recipe, so they do not\n * read it.\n * The range sits on glass's quiet TRACK, whose tone follows the SCHEME (light\n * track in light, dark in dark), not the plate. So its ink is the scheme's ink,\n * `--foreground`. Pass 2 took `--ink-muted` halfway toward `--primary`; both of\n * those are certified against the PLATE and flip with it, so on a dark plate\n * in the light scheme (the owner brick, lab(38% 32 24)) the bar went near-white\n * on the light track: 2.42 on Extract and 2.19 on the Atmosphere well, under\n * the 3:1 graphics floor (pass-03 `ink-candidates.jsonl`). `--foreground`\n * holds 5.23 or better on every measured cell, both schemes; any mix toward\n * `--primary` that keeps the hue falls under 3:1 on the owner brick by 25%. */\n\n:root {\n    --slider-range-bg: var(--foreground);\n}\n\n/* THE GUARDED LETTERFORM RAMP recipe (T.W6 · W6-4 — Q5 RULED, owner-verbatim:\n * \"Only palettes should be rainbow--the letterforms dropdown and the title\";\n * T-43 owner-CONFIRMS). The ONE recipe for the exactly-TWO consume sites\n * (DockViewSelect's \"Palettes\" entry + PalettesPane's title letterforms) —\n * never a scoped twin (the S.W7-7 lesson). Stops are the THREE root tokens\n * `boot/useViewAccents` writes from the ONE resolver\n * (`@composables/color/palettes-ramp` — derived from the live accent,\n * gamut-guarded, each site's WCAG floor); the guard's output IS O-14's T-10\n * referent. C3-ledger: the sanctioned exception to the nav ink law (Q18).\n * Fallbacks = the resolver's own pre-first-write class of value (the\n * `--accent-view` @property initial family), overwritten at first resolve. */\n\n.palettes-ramp-text {\n    background-image: linear-gradient(\n        90deg,\n        var(--palettes-ramp-0, oklch(0.632 0.214 333.5)),\n        var(--palettes-ramp-1, oklch(0.632 0.214 13.5)),\n        var(--palettes-ramp-2, oklch(0.632 0.214 53.5))\n    );\n    /* X-DS value pass 4 (P4R-01): the stops sit at their hues' gamut maximum,\n     * so the run between them walks the hue wheel (OKLCh) rather than cutting\n     * through the grey middle of sRGB. The line above stays for engines\n     * without gradient interpolation spaces. */\n    background-image: linear-gradient(\n        in oklch 90deg,\n        var(--palettes-ramp-0, oklch(0.632 0.214 333.5)),\n        var(--palettes-ramp-1, oklch(0.632 0.214 13.5)),\n        var(--palettes-ramp-2, oklch(0.632 0.214 53.5))\n    );\n    -webkit-background-clip: text;\n    background-clip: text;\n    color: transparent;\n}"]}
